   "evidence": "mathlib/Mathlib/LinearAlgebra/Matrix/PosDef.lean:54 `variable [CommRing R'] [PartialOrder R'] [StarRing R']`; :355 `theorem dotProduct_mulVec_zero_iff [StarOrderedRing R'] [IsProperStar R'] ... : star x \u2b1d\u1d65 A *\u1d65 x = 0 \u2194 A *\u1d65 x = 0`. Block.lean lines 45\u201355 use `toEuclideanLin` only to unwrap to and re-wrap from `*\u1d65` (`hx'`, `hb`). `DecidableEq` enters only through `toEuclideanLin` (PiL2.lean:1216).",
   "file": "TauCeti/Analysis/Matrix/PosSemidef/Block.lean",
   "fix": "Add a `mulVec` lemma over that general `R'`, e.g. `theorem toBlocks\u2081\u2082_mulVec_eq_zero (hS : S.PosSemidef) {x : \u03ba \u2192 R'} (hx : S.toBlocks\u2082\u2082 *\u1d65 x = 0) : S.toBlocks\u2081\u2082 *\u1d65 x = 0`, plus its `Sum.swap` twin. Then derive the `toEuclideanLin` kernel inclusions from it as one-line corollaries. The range inclusions stay at `RCLike`, since they need adjoints.",
   "issue": "`ker_toEuclideanLin_toBlocks\u2082\u2082_le` (and its swapped form `ker_toEuclideanLin_toBlocks\u2081\u2081_le`, line 61) requires `[RCLike \ud835\udd5c]`, `toEuclideanLin` and `[DecidableEq \u03ba]`. The proof first converts to the plain statement `S.toBlocks\u2082\u2082 *\u1d65 x = 0 \u2192 S.toBlocks\u2081\u2082 *\u1d65 x = 0` and then calls `dotProduct_mulVec_zero_iff`, which Mathlib states for any `CommRing R'` with `PartialOrder`, `StarRing`, `StarOrderedRing` and `IsProperStar`. So the core fact is under-generalized.",
   "line": 41
  }
 ],
